From 2d9da33e808332f9fdb2b856b5ad9c94d928c828 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:21:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Font: glyphs placed to the pixel (Makefile FONT=original|a|b,
 default original); rows a screen cuts into pieces in the original's cells

drawGlyph places a glyph in a 16-pixel cell shifted by x & 3 and keeps the columns it shares with the previous glyph's
cell; spaces are the font's blank glyph, tabs and position codes clear from the next grid cell. Rows that the menus cut
at the original's offsets (packed labels such as YearDay, the digits row renderNumber copies, the tournament calendar,
the shop's bits and confirm boxes, the keeper header, the curling options) are laid out in the original's cells
(FONT_CELLS, DRAW_STRING_CELLS, TEXTBOX_IN_CELLS). Numbers pad with a figure space as wide as a digit. FONT=original
compiles the original code: the executable is byte for byte the one without this patch.
---
